# No deprecated code

Aligns with diary **2026-10-10 — Datenmodell — kein deprecated** and [`requirements-code.md`](../../_docs/requirements/requirements-code.md) (*No deprecated APIs*). ESLint also enforces **`@typescript-eslint/no-deprecated`** on *consuming* deprecated third-party/TS APIs — see [`eslint.mdc`](./eslint.mdc).

## Forbidden in `src/**`

- **`@deprecated` JSDoc** (or comments that mark APIs/constants as deprecated).
- **Exported compatibility aliases** — old name re-exported beside the new name (`rebuildBlock` → `rebuildRigidPrimitive`, type aliases, renamed constants).
- **Symbols or files whose sole purpose is “use X instead”** — update imports/call sites, then delete the old surface.

## Allowed

- **One-shot load migration** — private constants + `migrate*` / `normalize*` (e.g. old preset IDs in saved JSON). No `@deprecated` tag; document allowed legacy keys in Requirements, not in source as deprecated APIs.
- **Tests** may use old **serialized payloads** to assert migration; prefer fixture names like `savedSceneWithRootShadowSoftness`, not “deprecated API”.

## When renaming or splitting APIs

1. Find all references (`grep` old symbol).
2. Switch call sites to the canonical name.
3. Remove the old export/alias in the same change set — do not leave a deprecated shim.

## Agent checklist

- Before adding a “temporary” alias: **don’t** — migrate callers instead.
- After refactors: `rg -i '@deprecated|deprecated' src/` must be **empty** (except if explicitly exempted in Requirements).
